{"generated":"2026-10-10 19:38","findings":[{"id":"pricing","severity":"high","title":"GPU pricing started on 2026-09-22; main-account allowances were not resized","paras":["Until 2026-09-22 a GPU job cost about one credit per CPU (a 32-GPU b200 job on 2026-08-18: 100 credits a minute; the same job now: 104,288). Since then each GPU type has its own price (a typical GPU job costs about 250\u00d7 more), but the standard main-account allowance stayed at 10,800,000 credits a month \u2014 now only about 96 H100-hours or 324 A100-hours. That is why so many main accounts ran out within days. (Project and condo accounts have no such allowance; they are limited only by GPUs at once.)","Ask: are the main-account allowances meant to be this small, or due to be resized?"],"tables":[]},{"id":"allowance","severity":"high","title":"Main accounts are told 1,000 GPU-hours; their credit allowance runs out long before","paras":["This is about each lab's main account \u2014 the one named after the PI (e.g. `ayuille1`) that everyone in the lab submits to by default. For it, `sbalance` shows 1,000 GPU-hours and 180,000 CPU core-hours, but a third limit on the same account \u2014 10,800,000 credits a month \u2014 always runs out first (table). It resets on the 1st; in between, used credits halve every 30 days (about 7.4 A100-hours of room back per day). `sbalance` also sums the whole quarter, so its numbers do not match what Slurm enforces.","Project and condo accounts are not affected: their credit budget is so large it never runs out, and what limits them is the number of GPUs they may hold at once."],"tables":[{"caption":"Standard JHU main-account allowance: 10,800,000 credits per month","cols":["Resource","Credits per hour","Hours per month","Compared with sbalance"],"rows":[["B300 GPU","221,820","49","5% of 1,000 GPU-hours"],["B200 GPU","195,540","55","6% of 1,000 GPU-hours"],["H200 GPU","120,600","90","9% of 1,000 GPU-hours"],["H100 GPU","112,560","96","10% of 1,000 GPU-hours"],["A