person may hold all of it; no lab has an account coordinator (0 on the cluster), so PIs cannot set limits for their own members.","What it costs the others (last 30 days): in 25 of 39 labs where 3+ people used GPUs, one person used more than half of the lab's GPU-hours; 41,342 GPU-hours were used beyond twice an equal share. 45 people in 14 labs waited 1,299 hours in all for their own project account while a single lab-mate held half or more of its GPUs. Since 2026-09-26, a lab going over its main allowance ended running jobs 316 times (1,437 jobs of 97 people; 41 times several people's jobs at once).","Suggestion \u2014 each piece is a standard feature Skipjack already uses somewhere (24 people have their own GPU cap on condo accounts; home folders have per-person quotas): (1) GPUs at once per person, e.g. half a project account (`MaxTRESPerUser=gres/gpu=8` on QOS `jhu`), and 2 GPUs / 8 hours for interactive sessions; (2) GPU-hours per person (`GrpTRESMins` on each person's association, e.g. about twice an equal share of a main allowance) \u2014 it fades over 30 days and resets on the 1st, so it is a monthly budget; a strictly weekly one needs a weekly reset script; (3) `safe` in AccountingStorageEnforce, so a job that would overrun a budget waits instead of being killed; (4) each PI coordinator of their own accounts, so labs can raise or lower these themselves; (5) a WEKA directory quota on each person's folder inside the lab directory (WEKA 4.4 has no per-user quotas)."],"tables":[{"caption":"Per-person limits today","cols":["Where","Per-person GPU cap","Per-person monthly / storage limit"],"rows":[["Main accounts (QOS `scavenger`)","none","none"],["Project accounts (`jhu`/`jhu2`/`jhu4`)","same as the account (16/32/64)","none"],["Condo accounts","same as the condo's size","none"],["Scratch / project storage","-","per lab directory only"],["Home directories","-","per person"]],"num":[]},{"caption":"Labs where one person used the most (last 30 days; people not nam