2","biol","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["sgoswam4","cise","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["sma76","apms","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["uchitra1","csci","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["zchiu1","csci","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["zli426","csci","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["zwang570","elce","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["zxiao25","csci","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,16,"12,228","38\u00d7"],["lgarci27","clsp","$20 (36 A100-h)",1,16,"11,940","37\u00d7"],["jperafa1","arch","$15 (27 A100-h)",1,16,"11,931","37\u00d7"],["svillar3","apms","$5,000 (9,009 A100-h)",0,"-","9,009","28\u00d7"],["tzaki1","meen","$180 (324 A100-h)",1,4,"3,300","10\u00d7"],["tshu2","csci","$50 (90 A100-h)",1,16,"1,892","6\u00d7"],["emallad1","elce","$200 (360 A100-h)",0,"-","360","1\u00d7"],["rdesouz4","arch","$100 (180 A100-h)",0,"-","180","1\u00d7"],["arochab1","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",1,16,"72","0\u00d7"],["bblanch6","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["bgermro1","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["dzarzhi1","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["ext-mwang131","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["jasonw","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["jbiondo2","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["kniebuh1","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["mwang131","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["sponoma1","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["twu73","arch","$20 (36 A100-h)",0,"-","36","0\u00d7"],["jsalt2026-lgarci27","clsp","no limit",0,"-","0","0\u00d7"]],"num":[3,4,5,6]}]},{"id":"capacity","severity":"high","title":"Project accounts, not main-account allowances, decide who gets the GPUs","paras":["Since 2026-09-22, the 52 JHU labs with project or condo accounts used 94% of all JHU GPU-hours; the 79 labs with only a main account used 6%. The GPUs-at-once caps add up to 1,444 GPUs against 340 in the JHU partitions, so a cap is not a guarantee: an active project account uses about 1,755 GPU-hours a month (median; busiest 10,503). `sbalance` shows each project as \"100,000,000 GPU-hours allocated\" \u2014 the source of claims of hundreds of millions of hours.","Project accounts also carry 556\u00d7 a main account's fairshare weight, so the same labs are first in line. Ask: tie caps and shares to the size of the approved allocation rather than to the number of accounts."],"tables":[{"caption":"GPU use since 2026-09-22, per month","cols":["Labs","Number of labs","Share of JHU GPU-hours","GPU-hours per lab per month"],"rows":[["With project/condo accounts",52,"94%","3,071"],["Main account only",79,"6%","124"]],"num":[1,2,3]}]},{"id":"billing","severity":"high","title":"Project accounts are set up to be billed to the PI; prices are not published","paras":["Main accounts run on the free QOS `scavenger` (free list: `all`, `scavenger`, `ssci`); the project QOS `jhu`/`jhu2`/`jhu4` are billable to the cost center a PI must attach before a project is created. Billing is enforced, but every rate is $0.00 today (ARCH: no billing without notice).","ARCH's cost preview reads the billing weights as 0.1 cent per hour, which implies the prices below: a typical active project would cost about $1,299 a month (top quarter $3,963 or more; busiest $22,005), and the standard main allowance is worth $180 (the submit tool calls it a \"weekly cap\" although it resets monthly). Ask: publish the rates, any cap per project or per PI, and whether main accounts stay free."],"tables":[{"caption":"Prices implied by today's billing weights (not yet charged)","cols":["Resource","Per GPU-hour (or core-hour)"],"rows":[["B300","$3.697"],["B200","$3.259"],["H200","$2.010"],["H100","$1.876"],["A100 SXM","$0.555"],["RTX PRO 6000","$0.555"],["L40S","$0.291"],["A100 MIG slice","$0.185"],["CPU core (med partition)","$0.0062"]],"num":[1]}]},{"id":"fairshare","severity":"medium","title":"Queue priority works against main accounts inside a department","paras":["Priority = fairshare (up to 20,000 points) + time waiting (up to 5,000, reached after 7 days) + job size (up to 5,000). Slurm ranks schools first, then departments, then the accounts inside a department by their shares: a main account has 180,000, a project or condo account 100,000,000 (556\u00d7). So main accounts rank behind project accounts that have used far more \u2014 right now 52 main accounts in 10 departments.","In csci (409 people) the median fairshare score is 0.109 on main accounts and 0.259 on project/condo accounts (2.4\u00d7) \u2014 about 3,002 priority points, or 4.2 days of waiting in the queue. School order right now: IT / ARCH-managed (0% of recent use) > Public Health (0% of recent use) > gp (0% of recent use) > jh (0% of recent use) > Medicine (0% of recent use) > Arts & Sciences (5% of recent use) > Engineering (94% of recent use)."],"tables":[{"caption":"Example: csci department. Each main account next to the busiest project account that is ranked ahead of it (rank 1 = starts first)","cols":["Main account","Its share of dept use","Its rank","Project account ahead of it","Its share of dept use","Its rank"],"rows":[["hhu49","0.4%","69 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["ayuille1","0.4%","68 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["bvandur1","0.4%","67 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["uchitra1","0.4%","66 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["aphill27","0.4%","65 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["ghadfie1","0.4%","64 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["zxiao25","0.4%","63 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["aliu74","0.3%","62 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["afield6","0.3%","61 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["munbera1","0.3%","60 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["tshu2","0.3%","59 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["pkoehn1","0.3%","58 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["mdredze1","0.3%","57 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["abhatt40","0.3%","56 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"],["jeisner1","0.3%","55 of 70","dkhasha1_safety","11.4%","47 of 70"]],"num":[1,4]}]},{"id":"storage","severity":"medium","title":"Storage limits are inconsistent","paras":["Scratch limits (/weka/scratch/jhu/PI or /weka/scratch/schmidt/PI) range from 1 TB to 70 TB with no obvious rule, and 14 directories have no limit at all (`arochab1`, `bblanch6`, `bgermro1`, `dzarzhitsky`, `ext-mwang131`, `jperafa1`, `kniebuh1`, `mprotzm2`, `rdesouz4`, `sponoma1`, `ssci-aviralku`, `ssci-jbt`, `ssci-rus`, `ssci-ys-shigroup`). Only 14 of 156 labs have a project filesystem (/weka/projects/PI, 500G to 160T). Not matching any lab's account: `admin`, `a user`, `a user`, `mallada`, `vandurme`."],"tables":[{"caption":"Scratch size limits","cols":["Limit","Number of labs"],"rows":[["1.0T",80],["2.0T",1],["3.0T",1],["4.0T",1],["5.0T",5],["6.0T",4],["8.0T",1],["10.0T",32],["20.0T",19],["50.0T",1],["70.0T",2]],"num":[1]},{"caption":"Nearly full (90% or more)","cols":["Storage","Lab","Used","Limit","Used %"],"rows":[["scratch","bvandur1","9.1T","10.0T","91%"],["scratch","dkhasha1","928G","1.0T","93%"],["scratch","dssg2026-ext-rghani1","18.1T","20.0T","90%"],["scratch","hbharad2","10.0T","10.0T","100%"],["scratch","jsalt2026-lgarci27","68.9T","70.0T","98%"],["scratch","mfalk1","1000G","1.0T","100%"],["scratch","mfazlya1","916G","1.0T","92%"],["scratch","munbera1","956G","1.0T","96%"],["scratch","mwyart1","5.0T","5.0T","99%"],["scratch","ssci-svlevine","19.9T","20.0T","100%"],["scratch","sxu83","929G","1.0T","93%"],["scratch","tlippin1","901G","1.0T","90%"],["scratch","tshu2","1.0T","1.0T","100%"],["scratch","tzaki1","911G","1.0T","91%"],["scratch","uchitra1","9.4T","10.0T","94%"],["scratch","ycao43","1000G","1.0T","100%"],["project","dkhasha1","90.8T","92.0T","99%"],["project","mwyart1","14.1T","15.0T","94%"]],"num":[2,3,4]},{"caption":"Project filesystems","cols":["Lab","Size","Used","Used %"],"rows":[["jgray21","160T","21.3T","13%"],["rchella4","150T","19.1T","13%"],["dkhasha1","92.0T","90.8T","99%"],["lshi40","70.0T","9.2T","13%"],["hbharad2","45.0T","16.9T","38%"],["mdredze1","40.0T","3.5T","9%"],["acharl15","30.0T","8.2K","0%"],["shayou1","30.0T","91.8G","0%"],["lisik3","25.0T","10.7T","43%"],["ychen756","20.0T","5.1T","25%"],["mwyart1","15.0T","14.1T","94%"],["tshu2","15.0T","5.7T","38%"],["mprotzm2","4.5T","8.2K","0%"],["kgligor1","500G","2.2G","0%"]],"num":[1,2,3]}]},{"id":"blocked","severity":"info","title":"177 of 604 GPUs (29%) cannot run jobs right now","paras":["Some nodes are held by admin reservations (testing, burn-in) or are down/draining. B200 and B300 nodes are only open to Schmidt accounts; the other GPU partitions only to JHU accounts."],"tables":[{"caption":"","cols":["Why","Nodes","GPUs"],"rows":[["Reservation `ssci-b300-eval`","gb302, gb303, gb304, gb305, gb306, gb307, gb308, gb309, gb310, gb311, gb312, gb313, gb314, gb315, gb316, gb317",128],["Reservation `ssci1-oct2026`","gb208, gb212",16],["Reservation `ssci4-oct2026`","gb202, gb215, gb216",24],["Reservation `ssci5-oct2026`","gb214",8],["idle + drain: XID issues needs AC cycle - BG","ga129",24],["mixed + planned","gb201",8],["mixed + planned","gb203",8],["mixed + planned","gb204",8],["mixed + planned","gb205",8],["mixed + planned","gb206",8],["mixed + planned","gb207",8],["mixed + planned","gb209",8],["mixed + planned","gb210",8],["mixed + planned","gb211",8],["idle + drain: reseat cable - BB","gb213",8],["mixed + planned","gb214",8],["mixed + planned","gh104",4],["mixed + planned","gh110",4],["idle + drain: Prolog error","gh111",4],["mixed + planned","gh118",4],["mixed + planned","gh128",4],["mixed + planned","gh131",4],["idle + drain: PCIe issue, needs cycle and reseat - BG : Not responding : reboot issued : reboot timed out","gh202",4],["idle + drain: NHC: Check check_nv_gpu_count 4 returned 1","gh203",4],["mixed + drain: draining for firmware updates - Kyle","gr102",4]],"num":[2]}]}],"glossary":[["Main account","The Slurm account named after the PI (e.g. `ayuille1`). Everyone in the lab submits to it by default. It has a monthly allowance of billing credits and no limit on GPUs at once, and its jobs are free (QOS `scavenger`)."],["Project account","An extra account a PI can request for a specific project, named PI_project (e.g. `jgray21_disc`). No practical monthly limit, but capped at 16 GPUs at once (32 or 64 for a few). Its jobs are billable to the project's cost center (rates are $0 today)."],["Cost center","A JHU budget number a PI attaches to a project in ARCH's portal; billable project usage would be charged to it."],["Implied price","ARCH's billing code treats each billing unit as 0.1 cent per hour, so the cluster's weights already imply a price list (e.g. A100 $0.555, H100 $1.876 per GPU-hour). Not charged today."],["Condo account","An account for GPUs a PI bought into (`*_h200`, `*_rtx6000`). It guarantees access to that many GPUs of that type."],["Billing credits","What Slurm charges a running job every minute (Slurm calls them billing-minutes). The price depends on the hardware: e.g. one H100 costs 1,876 credits per minute, one A100 555."],["Monthly allowance","The number of credits a main account may spend per calendar month, shared by everyone in the lab. It resets on the 1st. When it runs out, new jobs on the main account wait (reason `AssocGrpBillingMinutes`). Only main accounts have one that matters: project and condo accounts have a credit budget so large it never runs out."],["Usage fading","Between resets, older usage slowly counts less: it halves every 30 days. A main account that has spent its allowance gets a small amount back each day."],["GPUs at once","A cap on how many GPUs an account (or one user) may hold at the same moment, regardless of how long they run. Project and condo accounts have one (16, 32 or 64); main accounts do not."],["Queue priority","When GPUs are busy, waiting jobs start in priority order. Up to 20,000 points come from fairshare, up to 5,000 from time spent waiting (full after 7 days), up to 5,000 from job size."],["Fairshare","The part of queue priority that rewards groups that have used little recently compared with their entitlement. Scored 0 to 1; higher starts sooner."],["Shares","A group's entitlement in the fairshare calculation, set by the admins. Only the ratio between groups competing at the same level matters: a main account has 180,000, each project or condo account 100,000,000."],["QOS","Quality of service: a named bundle of limits attached to an account (e.g. `jhu` = 16 GPUs at once)."],["Partition","A group of nodes with the same GPU type, e.g. `h100`, `a100`."],["Reservation","Nodes set aside by the admins (maintenance, testing, burn-in); ordinary jobs cannot use them."],["GPU tiers","High = B300, B200, H200, H100. Mid = A100, RTX PRO 6000. Low = L40S and A100 MIG slices. Based on the cluster's own price per GPU."],["MIG slice","A fraction of an A100 (2g.20gb = 20 GB) offered on the `interactive_gpu` partition."]]}